+### 2026-08-30 — Degraded safe DNS reuses the accepted M1 resolver without fallback (TASK-260715-2zmw58)
+- DECISION: M2 degraded mode accepts both tunnel-owned UDP and TCP DNS but sends every upstream query through the existing M1 DNS-over-TCP `direct-tcpip` path to the generation-global active ordered numeric `dns53` endpoint. Port defaults to 53; endpoint family order is the stored order; DoH, discovery, product/system/physical resolver fallback, fake DNS, and per-query family racing remain absent.
+- READINESS: `DNSConsumerFactory.prepareSafeDNS(...)` must establish one current SSH-opened endpoint before M1 settings, while public degraded `(1,1,0)` additionally requires the current `BaseReady(g)` proof after settings, packet reads, and mandatory health recheck. Mandatory safe-DNS exhaustion clears usable bits and settings; it cannot trigger relay reprobe or any physical fallback.
+- EVIDENCE GATE: ADR-022 deliberately contains no numeric DNS defaults. Existing `TASK-260721-3miqh4` remains non-production-authorized, so production composition fails before routes with `production_policy_unauthorized`; this task does not copy candidate values or create a second research owner. The existing downstream DAG is complete and nonredundant; no task or dependency edge was added.
+- BOARD ANOMALY: `task-board validate` returned exit 0 while reporting `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for out-of-scope `STORY-260715-1y04r0`: it is stored as `backlog` while child `TASK-260720-1qhxqa` is `development`. A scoped activity read returned exit 1 because no activity resource exists; that absence was not treated as provenance evidence. This task did not mutate the mismatched Story or its children, and the board-wide gate remains recorded as failing for the orchestrator to route separately.
